{
 "why": "A callsign said right before a distance (#648, #650's follow-up): a number word too big to be a distance on final is never glued onto the flight number before it (JetBlue 123 25 miles out: JBU123); a short flight and its distance read as before when both readings are on ADS-B (JetBlue 12 4 mile final, JBU12 and JBU124 around: JBU12); a written flight whose distance digit was lost keeps its digits (JBU1234 mile final: JBU1234, not JBU1); with nothing on ADS-B, a short flight stays short (JetBlue 45 2 miles out: JBU45). Then a written flight keeps its digits with a shorter one on ADS-B (JBU1234 3 mile final, JBU12 around: JBU1234), and a flight number said in groups before a distance too big for final is joined (JetBlue 12 34 mile final: JBU1234).",
